 "glossary": "Filesystem. One command per line: <verb> <noun> [values] [key=value]. Word order is free; plurals are fine. Quote paths or text containing spaces or command words.\n  file   read <path> [head=N] [tail=N] | read legacy <path> (deprecated) | write <path> <content> | edit <path> edits='[{\"oldText\":..,\"newText\":..}]' [dry=true] | move <src> <dest> (also rename) | search <path> <glob> [exclude=a,b] | info <path>\n  media  read <path>  (image/audio/binary as base64)\n  multiple file  read <path1,path2,...>\n  dir    create <path> | list <path> | list size <path> [sort=name|size] | info <path> | move <src> <dest>\n  tree   <path> [exclude=a,b]  (recursive JSON tree)\n  allowed dir  (list allowed directories)\nExamples: read file notes/a.md head=20 | write file notes/todo.md \"Buy milk\" | search file src \"**/*.ts\" exclude=node_modules | list allowed dirs",
